      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9b67f5cef5e093621bca3439b1f555677415b2e619d1fc60f467dfca91e9c5c3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Short-interval moments and maxima can be compared through multiscale prime fields. Equal-variance prime blocks turn a large value into coordinated gains across scales; a mesh count with near/far second-moment decomposition tests whether high points are numerous enough and nonredundant; and partition-function and interval-scale moment profiles place bulk mass, barriers, and extrema in a common phase-transition framework.",
