    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9bd0b6e9b1ee57ddf64f063304b5680b9fb1cd1d216b801ba02f45c76ff92d28",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A compatible upper-bound architecture first replaces log zeta by a one-sided prime-supported majorant whose horizontal shift cancels a nonnegative zero term, then divides the prime polynomial into scale blocks. Different power budgets for different block lengths and direct truncated exponential moments reconcile accurate long approximation with the short powered lengths required for time-average diagonal control.",
