    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a2f9710659a06cdfa46f79936e5ebc42ffe4baceb4e54e8023039128d15db5d6",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Pair correlation has an exact energy representation: a two-zero statistic becomes a kernel-weighted L2 norm of a one-parameter exponential sum. In one direction, extending its frequency range requires main-order shifted von Mangoldt correlations; in the other, sufficiently uniform zero-energy control bounds short-interval prime variance, into which large prime gaps inject nonnegative mass. These are complementary transfers, not inverse theorems.",
