      "proposed_content": "Long Dirichlet-polynomial models retain off-diagonal interactions that a coefficient norm discards, relocating the higher-moment problem into shifted divisor correlations. Multidimensional circle-method analysis then stratifies those correlations by coupled rational directions, with discrepancies measuring near-resonance so that distinct main-term families are not averaged together.",
